### per-identity lists
acme  -> git.spike (listed)      : connect=200 http=200
acme  -> other.spike (not listed): connect=403 http=000
globex-> other.spike (listed)    : connect=200 http=200
globex-> git.spike (not listed)  : connect=403 http=000
no credential                    : connect=407 http=000
wrong password                   : connect=407 http=000
### gateway resolver through level 1, one tunnel per call
git.spike : {"bytes":65,"class":"ok","err":"","ms":4,"proto":"v2","sha":"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567"}
real host : {"bytes":67,"class":"ok","err":"","ms":331,"proto":"v2","sha":"ebdc087dc99d68bb340c282b2ba5f722def28d19"}
denied    : {"bytes":0,"class":"policy_denied","err":"CONNECT 403","ms":1,"proto":"v2","sha":""}
### the credential works from any pod that can reach the proxy
same credential from another container:      778 bytes body (empty body is success; an error prints text)
### SSRF: stock Squid with no address rule, allowlist contains a name that resolves privately, and literals
rebind.spike -> 172.30.0.20  : connect=200 http=200
literal 127.0.0.1            : connect=503 http=000
literal 169.254.169.254      : connect=000 http=000
literal not on the list      : connect=403 http=000
--- with the contract's address rule
rebind.spike -> 172.30.0.20  : connect=403 http=000
literal 127.0.0.1            : connect=403 http=000
literal 169.254.169.254      : connect=403 http=000
git.spike still allowed      : connect=200 http=200
### server-name fronting: CONNECT to a listed host, TLS and Host naming an unlisted one
acme, inner other.spike      : connect=200 http=200
